# Uservoice

> Uservoice is a customer intelligence and product feedback platform that helps software and SaaS companies collect, analyze, prioritize, and act on customer feedback to build better products.

Uservoice was founded in 2008 and is headquartered in San Francisco. It serves over 70,000 product innovators, with customers including Microsoft and Cisco. The platform centralizes feedback from every channel, enriches it with customer and revenue data, and uses AI-powered analytics to surface themes, priorities, and actionable insights for product teams.

## Core Purpose

Uservoice exists to turn scattered customer feedback into meaningful intelligence that guides smarter product decisions. It connects the voice of the customer to product strategy — so teams build what matters most, not what's loudest.

## Key Capabilities

### Feedback Collection
- Centralized feedback hub that ingests input from multiple channels (in-app widgets, web portals, email, integrations)
- Feedback forums where customers submit ideas and vote on existing requests
- SmartVote: a comparison-based voting mechanism that avoids vote fatigue and produces more reliable prioritization signals
- Microsurveys and guided validation studies for targeted research
- Bulk import via CSV or API for migrating historical data

### Feedback Intelligence (AI-Powered Analytics)
- **Topic Detection**: Automatically identifies recurring topics across all feedback using natural language processing
- **Theme Tracking**: Groups feedback into digestible themes and tracks how they evolve over time
- **Sentiment Analysis**: Interprets customer emotions and urgency signals to identify at-risk accounts and churn indicators
- **Urgency Alerts**: Categorizes ideas and comments by intensity of sentiment to surface critical issues early
- **Trend Analysis**: Monitors how feedback patterns shift across time, customer segments, and product areas
- **Auto-summarization**: Automatically summarizes and surfaces the most important ideas across large volumes of feedback

### Prioritization & Product Planning
- Ranks ideas by customer impact, revenue influence, account size, and demand volume
- Attaches user, account, and revenue data to every idea automatically
- Segments feedback by customer type, plan tier, or account to understand relative demand
- Produces impact reports and customer-backed recommendations for roadmap decisions

### Customer Engagement & Closing the Loop
- Enables teams to respond to customers directly and in bulk about the status of their requests
- Notifies customers when their requested features ship or move forward
- Reduces "black hole" perception — customers see their feedback was received, considered, and acted on
- Users who participate in feedback programs are approximately 20% more likely to become promoters (NPS improvement)

### Collaboration & Workflow
- Centralizes customer context so cross-functional teams (Product, CS, Sales) share the same data
- Aligns product strategy discussions with real customer evidence
- Slack notifications for product launch issues, bugs, and trending feedback
- Shared dashboards and reporting for stakeholder communication

